9,0 $ Growing on Paxillus (Tapinella) the photo below is of Paxillus involutus. $ This mushroom is the same as attackes Boletes so use the bolete part of the key to get the ED.
9,0 $ Growing on Pholiota, brownish in color $ Hypomyces succineus
9,0 ,n $ Its perithecia pimples are buff to brownish but the area around them is whitish to light buff Asci 100-135 X 5-6 µm . Ascospores 14-20 X 3.5-5 µm . The anamorph is Verticillium succineum. It is white to cream. Conidia 6.5-15 X 3-4.5 µm .
9,0 $ Growing on Pleurotus ostreatus, the Oyster Mushroom - a yellowish colored slime mold $ Physarum polycephalum
9,0 ,n $ It can also grow on other mushrooms such as Polyporus badius and also non mushroom areas. Its spores are globe like and 9-1 l µm .
9,cs8 $ Growing on Russula $ See A-B Below

9,0 $ Growing on the gills of Tubaria furfuraceae and distorting them, other parts are not affected. A whitish colored mold $ Nectriopsis tubariicola
9,0 ,n $ The Ascospores are 12-16 X 3-4 µm . The anamorph may be Verticillum.
9,0 $ Although not technically growing on a gilled mushroom this fungi often attacks inoculated Shiitake (Lentinula edodes) logs but can also grow on fallen rotting logs or bark. It is reddish brown to brownish when mature $ Hypocrea pachybasioides
9,0 ,n $ Its asci are 70-100 X 4-6.5 µm . Distal part ascospores 3-4.5 X 2.5- 4.5 µm . Proximal part ascospores 3.5-5.5 X 2.5-3.5 µm Conidia 2-4 X l-3 µm . Its anamorph is Trichoderma polysporum.
9,0 $ Although not technically growing on a gilled mushroom this fungi often attacks inoculated Shiitake (Lentinula edodes) logs that have or had Shiitake on them. They can also grow on Hypoxylon truncatum and Hypoxylon rubiginosum in other locations without the Shiitake. The attackers are black colored $ Nitschkia confertula
9,0 ,n $ Asci 32-40 X 5-7 µm . Ascospores 7-9 X 3.5-5 µm .

 10,0$ with spindle shaped spores 30-60 µm long.$ Spinellus fusiger
 10,0$ with ovoid spores 20-30 µm long. $ Spinellus chalybeus
 10,0$ with limnoform (lemon shaped) spores 20-40 µm long$ Spinellus macrosporus
10,0$ Other Species include : /// Spinellus sphaerosporus spores globe shaped approx. 10 µm///Spinellus gigasporus 12-15 X 50-60 µm.///Spinellus arvernensis 18-39 X 60-80 µm
