13,0 $ Growing on Coral Mushrooms. I have only found it on 2 species Clavulina cristata and Clavulina cinerea $ Helminthosphaeria clavariarum
13,0 ,n $ It is grayish turning darker to black. Typically it starts at the base of the coral mushroom and the parasite works up and can eventually cover the entire host. Its ascospores are 11-16X5- 7.5 µm . Its old name was Spadicioides clavariae. The anamorph is Diplococcium clavariarum. Conidia 13-28 X 6-9 µm .

