rem$  18,cs25 $ Growing on a mushroom that can not be seen, all we can see is a Squamanita 


19,0 $ Growing on the Splash cup Cyathus striatus forming a whitish becoming beige colored thick ring around it $ Hypocrea latizonata
19,0 ,n $ The pimples are orangish. There is no known anamorph. Distal part Ascospores 3.5-4 X 3-3.5 µm . Proximal part ascospores 3.5-4.5 X 2-3 µm . It is eastern North America in range.

20,0 $ Growing on Aleurodiscus amorphus, jelly like and creamy white in color, sometimes with pinkish tones, the tree the host fungi grows on is spruce or balsam fir $ Tremella simplex
20,0 ,n $ Basidiospores 7-9 diam. Conidia 4-7 X 2.5-5 µm ._: It may also grow on A. thujae. The Parasite grows in North America and Europe.
20,0 $ Growing on the crust Acanthophysellum lividocoeruleum= Corticium lividocoeruleum = Aleurodiscus lividocoeruleus $ Tremella subencephala
20,0 ,n $ Spores 6 X 4 µm . It is also reported on Aleurodiscus lividocoeruleus.
20,0 $ Growing on Aleurodiscus grantii $ Tremella mycetophiloides
20,0 ,n $ _ : It may also grow on A. simplex.

21,0 $ Growing on the Xylobolus frustulatus common name Ceramic Parchment and Xylobolus subpileatus $ Hypomyces xyloboli
21,0 ,n $ Its perithecia pimples are brownish colored, KOH has no reaction on them. Asci 110-126 X 5-6 µm . Ascospores 15-18 X 3.5-4.5 µm . Do not confuse with the typically orange colored Hypomyces aurantius which has been reported on Xylobolus subpileatus. Anamorph Cladobotryum sp. is gray-green colored. Conidia 8-14 X 5-6 µm .……………………………………….


30,0$ Jelly like, growing on Peniophora sp. A crust Fungi $ Tremella mesenterica=Tremella lutescens 
30,0 ,n $ -The Witches Butter. It is faint yellowish to yellowish orange colored. Jelly like. Spores 9-18 X 8-12 µm . Typically on hardwood. A favorite host is Peniophora aurantiaca.











