cs31,0$ Growing on the Earth Tongue

1,0$ Growing in North America.$ Hypomyces papulasporae var. americanus
1,0,n $   Asci 75-125 X 4-5.5 µm . Ascospores 13-17X2.5 4 µm , Asci 75-130 X 4-5.5 µm .
1,0$ Growing in Europe$ Hypomyces papulasporae var.papulasporae 
1,0,n $    Papulaspores not as large as American collections but the conidia are larger



cs2,0$ Growing on Polypores 
1,0$  Growing on the pore surface of Fomes fomentarius. It is whitish to cream in color often with pinkish tones. Its pores are often angular and 5-7 per mm.. $ Junghuhnia nitida 
1,0,n $    It is occasionally found growing on the fomes but typically without a fungal host just on wood. Its spores are 2-4.5 X 2-3 µm .
1,0$  Growing on Ganoderma, Fomes and Rigidoporus such as R. lineatus and R. microporus, looking fan shaped like a Chinese folding fan or like a upside down umbrella variable. $ Sporophagomyces chrysostomus Hypomyces chrysostomus. 
1,0,n $    It can be whitish to creamy yellow or with pinkish and can be fuzzy or more solid. It often can be peeled off its host. Asci 80-100 X 5-6 µm . Ascospores 9.5-15 X 3-4 µm . Its anamorph is Acremonium lindtneri. Conidia 10-25 X 25 µm . _: There is only one other species in this genus Sporophagomyces lanceolatus which looks similar but its ascospores are 30-36 X 35 µm , only on Rigidoporus and in Puerto Rico, and perhaps S. moellerianus./// sometimes they grow on themselves.
1,0$  Growing on Ganoderma and Laetiporus but also others, with yellowish in color, yellowish orange and yellowish brown, and pimpled resembling Hypocrea americana $ Hypocrea pulvinata 
