1,0$  Growing on Trichaptum, a hand lens is often needed to see the black colored stalked heads that grow on top of some of them $ Phaeocalicium polyporaeum 
1,0,n $    The black hairs resemble matchsticks hence the common name Match Stick Fungi They are about 1/16 inch tall. The Violet Tooth Polypore Trichaptum biforme is a favorite host, but also on T. abietinum. It is fairly commonly collected on T biforme
1,0$  Growing on Trichaptum looks whitish around the buff to yellowish colored occasionally a light brownish color, perithecia pimples and whitish and more fuzzy and threadlike elsewhere $ Hypomyces sibirinae 
 1,0,n $    a southeastern US Species. Also on Polyporus sp. Asci 110-130 X 4.5-6.5 µm . Ascospores 14-20 X 3.5-4.5 µm . Anamorph Cladobotryum hughesii. Conidia 10-30 X 3.5-6 µm .
1,0$  Growing on and covering both the upper and lower surface of Tyromyces/Oligoporus, not jelly like $ Hypocrea pallida 
1,0,n $    It also grows on other mushrooms but easiest to ID on the host above. It looks orangish colored but can be white in places it can also be light yellowish. The perithecia are orange and turn reddish with a drop of KOH. Asci 5.4-6.2 X 2.5-3 µm . Distal part ascospores 2.5-3 X 2-2.5 µm , proximal part-ascospores 3.0-3.5 X 2.0-2.5 µm . Conidia 25.5 X l2 µm . Its anamorph is believed to be Gliocladium penicillioides. Page 44
