1,0$  Growing on polypores, typically found when orange colored, has perithecia pimpled looking, turns reddish purple to purplish with a drop of KOH. Hosts include Stereum and Trametes versicolor $ Hyponiyces aurantius
1,0,n $    It can cover the pores or entire host mushroom. Asci 100-160 X 6-7 µm . Ascospores 20-25 µm x 4-6 µm . The white colored anamorph is Cladobotryum varium. Hosts include Trametes versicolor. Conidia 10-20 X 6-8 µm .  _: Hypoinyces subiculosus looks similar but grows in the southern North America and not northern. Its ascospores differ by being 1416 X 4-6 µm .  Page 45
1,0$  Growing on polypores, white to whitish or cream or buff to peach in color and can have yellowish tones and can have smaller whitish splotches, and crusty on polypores it does not turn reddish with KOH drop on its surface $ Hypomyces mycophilus
1,0,n $    In this the teleomorph state it is basically found on polypores such as Trametes versicolor but occasionally others, there are only 5 collections of the teleomorph so it is rare. The perithecia pimples are orangish to peach colored or with brownish tones. Asci 140-150 X 4-6 µm . Ascospores 1624 X 5-6.5 µm . _ also grows on Stereum. The anamorph is Cladobotryum polypori, which is buff in color and looks like cotton. Conidia 1424 X 7.5-10 µm . The anamorph also grows on other species including gilled mushrooms, tooth fungi, polypores and Stereum etc. Chlamydospores 20-30 X 1826 µm . ALSO _ the key for this one could use some work since it is not listed in this key on its other hosts
1,0$  Growing on polypores especially the Hemlock Varnish Shelf - Ganoderma tsuagae. It is greenish to blackish green. Also reported to be a dark brown but I have never seen it this color. It is roundish $ Hypocrea lixii 
