Cs6,0$ Growing on Lactarius
1,0$  Typically found in an orange to reddish colored stage, and typically covering entire host. Under the loop it looks pimpled $ Hypomyces
1,0$  Typically found in an orange to reddish colored stage, and typically covering entire host. Under the loop it looks pimpled $ Ilyponiyces lactifluonim 
1,0,n $    The Lobster Mushroom can start off whitish but is seldom found in this color. Typically it is found orangish colored but age's reddish and can then get purplish tones. For a more accurate macroscopic ID look for the orange stage, since several lookalikes share the white stage but do not turn orange or red. Asci 200-260 X 6 lO µm . The Ascospores are 3548 X 4.5-8 µm . Also Grows on Russula. It is unknown if it has an anamorph. KOH makes the pimple purple. Edible and Choice
1,0$  White to whitish occasionally buff covering the gills and at least some of the stalk but often not the entire host stalk. Basically a white lobster mushroom that stays white $ Hypomyces macrosporus
1,0,n$ A drop of KOH will not make it turn red or purple. This species is a good edible. Asci 200-270 X 7.5-10 µm . The ascospores are 3242 X 5-7 µm . It is not known if it has an anamorph. This mushroom can not typically be told apart from Hypomyces banningiae macroscopically but Hypomyces macrospores ascospores differ by having a line through the center of them like a pill.

1,0$  ) Typically white to whitish colored but turning yellowish colored then buff with age and drying. Growing on the underside of the caps covering the gills. The gills become fused together forming a solid mass. Typically the caps and lower stalks are not affected. Affected mushrooms seem much harder than their unaffected counterparts $ Hypomyces lateritius =Byssonectria lateritia macrosporus 
1,0,n$  = Peckiella lateritia. Asci 90-155 X 4 8 µm . Its Ascospores are 16-28 X 3 5-6 µm . Hosts include Lactarius uvidus, Lactarius camphoratus and other Lactarius. The perithecia pimples turn yellowish with KOH. The suspected anamorph is Acremonium tulasnei but it can be found before the pimples are formed. It also differs by being cottony and the mushroom is less firm then. Conidia 57 X 4.5-6.5 µm . Compare to Hypomyces lithuanicus = H. torminosus that can have a more cinnamony color and its pimples turn reddish with KOH
1,0$  ) Typically irregularly spider web like to cottony covering the gills. Whitish colored $ Hypomyces ochraceus or the Anamorph 
1,0,n$ see more below to tell the 2 apart

1,0$ Hypomyces armeniacus. Hosts can include both Russula and Lactarius and Clitocybe clavipes. The teleomorph Hypomyces ochraceous that is vary rarely found and his the pimple look, it is typically when found fallen on soil or debris after the mushroom disappears or has almost gone, but where the remains would be, it is beige with white sometimes orangish pimples. Asci 170-180 X 6-8 µm . Ascospores are 32-40 X 5-8 µm . Conidia 10-25 X 6-14 µm . The anamorph is the more common of them and is Cladobotrum verticillatum is what we typically find on the host mushrooms.

1,0$  Typically a solid whitish or white to buff covering over the hosts gills. Make sure to compare with Hypomyces macrosporus but this is different microscopically. It is not cobweb like $ Hypomyces banningiae 
1,0,n$ Grows in the East. Asci 210-320 X 6-9 µm . The ascospores are 30-42 X 57 µm . A drop of KOH will not make it turn red or purple. There is no known anamorph. One of the reported hosts in Lactarius piperatus. This mushroom is uncommon to rare. Hypomyces banningiae This mushroom can not typically be told apart from IT. macrosporus but Hypomyces macrospores ascospores differ by having a line through the center of them like a pill.
