rem$ 1,0 $ Growing on a tooth fungi Steccherinum adustum = Mycorrhaphium adustum. It is typically found when orangish colored and peritecia pimpled looking but can occasionally be whitish then reddish when mature $ Hypomyces aurantius 
rem$ 1,0 ,n $  Also grows on Polypores such as Trametes. It can cover the pores or teeth or the entire host fungi. When finding it on Steccherinum I typically see it only covering the teeth and have to turn the mushroom over to spot it. It turns reddish purple to purplish with a drop of KOH. Asci 100-160 X 6-7 µm . Ascospores 20-25 µm x 4-6 µm . The white colored anamorph is Cladobotryum varium. Conidia 10-20 X 6-8 µm .Hypomyces subiculosus looks similar but grows in the southern North America and not northern. Its ascospores differ by being 1416 X 4-6 µm .
